From 19ff02cd2ac42c724402fbfe95d2449c863f1be0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zswll2 <zswll2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 18:49:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 17/32] fix(desktop): remove edge-swipe drawer gesture
 (conflicts with iOS back)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

User ruling: the edge hot-zone swipe fights the browser's own back gesture
on iOS, so the whole gesture goes — not a flag, the code. Deletes the
classifyEdgeSwipe/drawerDragProgress pure functions, their tests, the
useEdgeSwipeDrawer hook (incl. gesture-target freeze and drag-follow
translateX), and the narrow overlay's settle timer, ghost drawer, and
drag-veil rendering. F4f's follow-finger animation is void with it.

Narrow drawer remains reachable via the titlebar sidebar button, backdrop
tap, and the >=44px in-drawer close button (all E2E-verified on
390x844 hasTouch; desktop 1280 docked sidebar unchanged).
